{ dg-modules "rcprelude" }
{ Rosetta Code, task "Input/Output for pairs of numbers", ALGOL 68 solution input-output-for-pairs-of-numbers-1.alg.
  https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Input/Output_for_pairs_of_numbers#ALGOL_68
  The text of Rosetta Code is available under the GNU Free Documentation
  License 1.3 (see README.md).  The solution is unchanged in orig/input-output-for-pairs-of-numbers-1.a68;
  this copy was prepared for ga68 and converted to SUPPER stropping by
  tools/rosetta_prep.py. }
access Rc_Prelude (
{ read a number from stand in then read and add that many pairs of numbers from stand in      }
{ and write the sum to stand out. If non integer data is supplied, a runtime error will occur }
to ( int n; read( ( n, newline ) ); n ) do
    int a, b;
    read( ( a, b, newline ) );
    print( ( a + b, newline ) )
od
)
